  "about": "The Seal Cave's deep passage (Book 9 sections 11 and 16; Stage 14, decisions S14-3, S14-8, S14-9 and S14-43): an interior of 48 x 20 tiles read tile for tile from docs/levels/sealcave_passage_tiles.txt by src/tools/levels/zones.ts, with no warp. Rock walls (`r`); the passage floor is wet rock open only on spring-tide days inside the tidal ground window (`n`); the knee-deep pool and the waist-deep lowest point are water (`w`, their bands marked as wades); the crawl's tiles are rock crawled through (marked); the fallen stone lies at P and slides north into its slot (marked, deep.stone). Its way in from Seal Cave's back wall and its way on into the Hollow Cairn are links: the cairn's tidal passage meets its west edge (the two interiors are placed side by side off the island grid by their origins), Seal Cave's back wall is a portal at A. The damp haze and the light off the water are fx props. Edit this plan, not the generated map, then run npm run zones.",
